---
pagination: { data: languages, size: 1, alias: lang }
permalink: "{{ '/' if lang == 'en' else '/es/' }}events/index.html"
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: events
titleKey: nav.events
ldType: CollectionPage
descKey: committee.events.meta_desc
pageScripts: ["/assets/js/committee.js"]
# the calendar file of this page's events (src/pages/events-ics.11ty.js), named in the page's <head> (base.njk)
calendarFeed: "/events.ics"
---
{#- Events: committee meetings (computed), monthly recurring events (config/site.yml `recurring_events:` — one
    La Viña holds — `host: lv`, its monthly workshop on Zoom — is with the GV & LV calendars, in La Viña's colour,
    online only: "Online on Zoom", Join online, its meeting ID; our own Grapevine Meeting is a NETA 65 one — its
    badge says so, never Grapevine's —, online only: "Online on Google Meet", its meeting code), Drive flyers with
    dated names, manual events, Texas GV/LV calendar events (a date we already show is left out by build_data).
    Since the list's redesign (November 2026: eleventy/filters/event-list.js evList, where every rule is explained)
    the page leads with what is NEW, phone first (a 390px phone used to scroll ~2,900px, past "Our monthly
    meetings" and the weekly meetings, to reach the first one-off event, and ~33,000px in all):
      · the shared hero, its "Save the date" card (the next Area assembly) beside it from 1024px and as the first card
        under it on narrower screens (side: "below");
      · below 1024px, "Next up" (#ev-nextup): the next three events, one line each, a link to its card;
      · the "Next 5 weeks" calendar (#ev-cal): from 1024px the sidebar, beside the list, in view while it scrolls;
        below 1024px folded under its heading near the top ("Show the calendar", with JavaScript — without it, it
        shows whole);
      · the filters (#ev-filters, with JavaScript only — without it every card shows): the kind (chips), the language
        it is held in, in person / online, the city and (when an event names one) the district — kept in the
        address (?kind=workshop&lang=es&mode=inperson&city=fort-worth&district=87), so a filtered view can be shared;
        the month chips jump to the months that show something under them;
      · the ONE-OFF events, month by month (a cancelled one until its day is over: a struck-through "Cancelled" card,
        its title to its notice page — eleventy/cancelled-pages.js); the years after the open ones folded behind
        "Show 2028 dates (n)" (committee.js eventsFold, cmEvents);
      · "Every month" (#ev-pinned): ONE card per monthly series — the next committee meeting (the dark card), the
        Grapevine Meeting (#ev-next-gvm), the CityWide booth, La Viña's workshop … —: how often, its next dates, what
        changed ("Nov 26 moved to Nov 18", "Dec 12: cancelled", "Not held on Dec 24") and "See all dates" (its series'
        page, /events/series/<key>/; the committee meeting's "All dates" its dates page, /events/series/committee-
        meeting/ — src/pages/events-committee.njk, since round 38 —, and "Meeting details" /meetings/#committee-meeting;
        the months that have only such dates keep their old #month-… anchors on "Every month"). Each date keeps its anchor
        there (#ev-recurring-citywide-dallas-2026-12-12: a link to it — the calendar's days, an event page's "See all
        events" — lands on its series' card), its own page, its entry in "Next 5 weeks" and in the .ics feeds;
      · "Every week" (#ev-weekly): the weekly open meetings; then past events, "How events get here", the calendar
        subscription (#subscribe) and, collapsed, "For committee members · Add an event" (ui.memberHelp,
        #how-events: the two kinds of flyers, the Drive folder, the naming rule + examples, the Portfolio's two Drive
        actions). With no NETA 65 events, the agenda's empty slot (#ev-empty-neta) points there.
    The hero's right-hand card ("Save the date"): the next Area assembly (event-tone.js isAssembly: never an ACM, a
    town hall or a GSR/DCM orientation) — else the next event from Grapevine's or La Viña's own calendars — never the
    first one-off event of the list below; its link goes to that event's own page (evHref,
    eleventy/filters/event-links.js). -#}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{%- set all = db.events.items | cmEvents(site, lang) | cmCollapseRecurring -%}
{%- set upcoming = all | where("past", false) -%}
{#- Past list: real one-off events only (a monthly meeting / booth date that has passed is not news — its calendar
    entry links to its own date page, /events/<its anchor>/, while events.json keeps it: committee.js detailsUrl) -#}
{%- set past = all | where("past", true) | whereNot("committee", true) | whereNot("recurring", true) | reverse -%}
{%- set meetings = upcoming | where("committee", true) -%}
{%- set next = meetings[0] -%}
{#- nNetaOwn — our NETA 65 events without the committee meetings: no flyer or event of ours yet (the empty state
    #ev-empty-neta, cmDriveChecked) -#}
{%- set nNetaOwn = upcoming | where("group", "neta") | length -%}
{%- set nCal = upcoming | where("group", "calendar") | length -%}
{%- set pageAbs = page.url | siteUrl(site) -%}
{%- set m = site.meeting -%}
{#- where the committee meeting is held, in the page's words ("Join on Zoom"): config/site.yml meeting.platform -#}
{%- set pf = { platform: m.platform or "Zoom" } -%}
{%- set di = db.status | cmDriveInfo(site) -%}
{%- set wos = db.weekly_open.items | cmWeeklyAll(lang) -%}
{%- set gm = site | cmSeriesNext("grapevine-meeting", lang, db.events.items) -%}
{#- the list: the one-off events by month, one card per series, "Next up", the filters' choices (evList) -#}
{%- set L = upcoming | evList(db, site, lang, wos) -%}

{#- evm.kindBadge(ev, kind): the kind of an event, in words and in its colour — macros/events.njk (an event's own page,
    event-share-leaf.njk, shows it too) -#}
{% import "macros/events.njk" as evm with context %}

{#- "Add to calendar" dropdown: evm.calMenu (macros/events.njk — since round 38 the committee meeting's dates page,
    src/pages/events-committee.njk, has it on each date too): brief Google / Outlook links in the page, the full ones
    once the menu opens; its note's words ONE copy on the agenda's <section> (data-cm-note-timed / data-cm-note-day) -#}

{#- An event's outside page (its organizers' — never its flyer): "Organizer's page ↗", so it is never taken for the
    title's link, which goes to the event's own page here (since the list's redesign; it said "Event details").
    .ev-org-btn: on a phone at larger text or relaxed spacing its icon steps aside and the ↗ may go under the word
    (areas/access.css, round 38b) -#}
{% macro organizerButton(ev, cls="btn-secondary btn-sm") %}
<a class="{{ cls }} ev-org-btn" href="{{ ev.link }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "external-link", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "evlist.organizer_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "evlist.organizer" | t(lang) }}</span> <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>
{% endmacro %}

{#- The anchors of a series' dates that its card does not list (the committee meeting's and the Grapevine Meeting's
    cards show one date, which rolls on in the browser): a link to any of them lands on the card — (round 38) an old
    shared link to a committee meeting's later date, opened, goes on to that date on its dates page (committee.js
    cmEvents: data-ev-dates; the first anchor is the date the card shows) -#}
{% macro dateAnchors(s) %}
{%- if s %}<span class="sr-only" aria-hidden="true" data-ev-date-anchors>{% for d in s.dates %}<span id="{{ d.anchor }}"></span>{% for a in d.item | evOldAnchors %}<span id="{{ a }}"></span>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}</span>{% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{#- What changed about a series' dates (evList notes): a date the host moved, a cancelled one, a month the rule skips -#}
{% macro seriesNotes(s, dark=false) %}
{%- if s and s.notes | length %}
<ul class="ev-series-notes{{ ' is-dark' if dark }}" role="list">
  {%- for n in s.notes %}
  {%- set nIcon = { cancelled: "calendar-x", moved: "calendar-sync", skipped: "calendar-minus" }[n.type] %}
  <li>{% icon nIcon, "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0" %}<span>
    {%- if n.type == "moved" %}<a class="link" href="#{{ n.anchor }}">{{ "evlist.note_moved" | t(lang, { from: n.from, to: n.to }) }}</a>
    {%- elif n.type == "cancelled" %}<a class="link" href="{{ n.href }}">{{ "evlist.note_cancelled" | t(lang, { day: n.day }) }}</a>
    {%- else %}{{ "evlist.note_skipped" | t(lang, { day: n.day }) }}{% endif -%}
  </span></li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{#- "Save the date": from the events with a date of their own (no committee meetings, a monthly series by its next
    date: cmCollapseRecurring's `later`), skipping the first of them — that one is near the top of the list anyway;
    the next Area ASSEMBLY (isAssembly: an ACM, the Area's town hall or a GSR/DCM orientation shares its colour but
    is not one) -#}
{%- set ahead = upcoming | whereNot("committee", true) | whereNot("later", true) -%}
{%- set sdPick = [] -%}
{%- for ev in ahead %}{% if loop.index0 > 0 and not sdPick.length and (ev | isAssembly) and sdPick.push(ev) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- for ev in ahead %}{% if loop.index0 > 0 and not sdPick.length and (ev.category == "gv-calendar" or ev.category == "lv-calendar") and sdPick.push(ev) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set sd = sdPick[0] -%}
{#- Structured data (schema.org): the upcoming events held at a place, for search engines' event listings —
    built by cmEventLd (eleventy/filters/committee.js eventLd, where every rule is explained): only events at a
    physical place with a postal address the public may attend (an online-only event gets none: this page, the .ics
    files and the events' own pages still show it), a monthly series by its next date. At the START of the page
    content, before the hero: Googlebot reads only the first 2 MB of a page's HTML. It is the first ld+json block in
    the page's <body> (tests read that one; the site's own graph comes before it, at the end of the <head>:
    base.njk). -#}
{%- set ldEvents = upcoming | cmEventLd(site, lang, pageAbs) -%}
{% if ldEvents | length %}<script type="application/ld+json">{{ { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": ldEvents } | rpJson | safe }}</script>{% endif %}
{% call(slot) ui.pageHero(lang, "nav.events" | t(lang), "committee.events.hero_sub" | t(lang), "calendar-days", "committee.events.eyebrow" | t(lang), { side: "below" }) %}
{%- if slot == "side" %}
  {%- if sd %}
  {%- set sdKind = sd | eventTone %}
  {% call ui.heroAside("committee.events.aside_title" | t(lang), lang, { id: "ev-aside-title", icon: "calendar-heart", href: sd | evHref(lang, db, site), linkLabel: "committee.events.aside_link" | t(lang) }) %}
  <div class="cm-ha-ev ev-tone-{{ sdKind }}">
    <span class="cm-ha-ev-tile{{ ' is-range' if sd.tile.range }}" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cm-tile-mon">{{ sd.tile.mon }}</span><span class="cm-ha-ev-day">{{ sd.tile.day }}</span><span class="cm-ha-ev-wd">{{ sd.tile.wd }}</span></span>
    <div class="cm-ha-ev-body">
      <p>{{ evm.kindBadge(sd, sdKind) }}</p>
      <p class="hero-aside-title mt-1.5">{{ sd.title }}</p>
      <p class="hero-aside-text mt-0.5">{{ sd.rangeLabel if sd.multiDay else sd.shareWhen }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endcall %}
  {%- endif %}
{%- else %}
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="btn-light" href="#subscribe">{% icon "calendar-sync", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.events.subscribe_btn" | t(lang) }}</a>
    <a class="btn-on-dark" href="{{ '/meetings/' | lurl(lang) }}#committee-meeting">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ "nav.meeting" | t(lang) }}</a>
  </div>
  {#- No hero stat: the committee sub-nav's Events tab counts the upcoming events, each once (a monthly series
      once, no committee meetings: upcomingEventEnds); the filter chips count the cards -#}
{%- endif %}
{% endcall %}

{% committeeNav lang, "events", db %}

<div class="container-page section pt-8 pb-0 sm:pt-12">
{#- ---------- Next up (below 1024px; the sidebar's calendar says it from there): the next events, one line each —
     a one-off event, or a series' next date — each a link to its card. Two spare lines wait hidden: as an event is
     over, the browser drops its line and shows the next (committee.js expire(): data-cm-expire, data-cm-max). ---------- -#}
{%- if L.nextUp | length %}
<section id="ev-nextup" class="ev-nextup lg:hidden" aria-labelledby="ev-nextup-title">
  <h2 id="ev-nextup-title" class="ev-nextup-h">{% icon "clock-3", "size-4" %}{{ "committee.events.cal_next_up" | t(lang) }}</h2>
  <ol class="ev-nextup-list" role="list" data-cm-max="{{ L.nextShown }}">
    {%- for ev in L.nextUp %}
    <li class="ev-tone-{{ ev | eventTone }}{{ ' hidden' if loop.index0 >= L.nextShown }}" data-cm-expire="{{ ev.expireIso }}"><a class="ev-nextup-item" href="#{{ ev.anchor }}"><span class="ev-nextup-day" aria-hidden="true"><span>{{ ev.tile.mon }}</span><span class="ev-nextup-n">{{ ev.tile.day }}</span></span><span class="min-w-0"><span class="ev-nextup-t">{{ ev.title }}</span><span class="ev-nextup-when">{{ ev.rangeLabel if ev.multiDay else ([ev.tile.wd, ev.timeLabel] | select | join(" · ")) }}</span></span></a></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>
{%- endif %}
<div class="ev-layout">
{#- ---------- "Next 5 weeks" (cmCalWeeks → committee.js calendarWeeks, where every rule is explained) ----------
     From 1024px the sidebar's top, beside the list (its sticky-aside wrapper keeps it in view under the header while
     the list scrolls: main.css; .ev-layout puts it in the right-hand column — committee.css); below 1024px, before the
     list (DOM order = phone order = Tab order: one copy, never moved), folded under its heading with JavaScript
     ("Show the calendar": [data-ev-cal-toggle], committee.js calendar()), whole without it.
     A month-style grid, Sunday first, of the five weeks from this one (Central time) — EVERY upcoming event of the
     page on each of its days (committee meetings, each date of a monthly series, an assembly on all its days) and the
     two weekly open meetings — plus three spare weeks, hidden: as each week ends, the browser drops its row and shows
     the next (committee.js expire(): the row's data-cm-expire is the moment its Saturday ends; the tbody's
     data-cm-max="5"), so five weeks always show between builds. A plain table (not role="grid"): Tab goes through the
     days that have something on, row by row, and a screen reader names each column's weekday. Each such day is a
     link to its first event's card (a series' date: its anchor on its series' card) holding the day's number, the
     whole day in words for screen readers and up to 3 dots in the events' colours (a weekly meeting's: a ring; more:
     "+n"); the 1st of a month (and the grid's first day) names its month. The build's today: .is-today +
     aria-current="date"; the days before it: .is-past, no link. Under the grid, the day's list (aria-live) — today's
     when something is on today, else the next day with something on ("Next up") —, each entry a link to its card.
     With JavaScript, picking a day shows that day's list instead of jumping; a link to a card the list hides
     (another filter, a month folded behind "Show more") is revealed by the list itself (cmEvents: on hashchange, and
     on "cm:reveal"). Every minute committee.js calToday() moves today and the past days on. Then the colour key of
     the dots and one line of help. data-lastmod="skip": the card changes with the day, not with the content
     (eleventy/lastmod.js). No card when nothing is on in these weeks (calendarWeeks: null). -#}
{%- set cal = upcoming | cmCalWeeks(wos, lang, { weeks: 5, spare: 3 }) %}
{% if cal %}
<aside class="ev-side-cal min-w-0" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.cal_title' | t(lang, { n: cal.n }) }}">
  <div class="sticky-aside">
    <section id="ev-cal" class="cm-cal-card card card-pad" data-cm-cal data-lastmod="skip" aria-labelledby="ev-cal-title">
      <div class="ev-cal-head">
        <div class="ev-cal-hd">
          <p class="eyebrow text-gv">{{ "committee.events.cal_eyebrow" | t(lang) }}</p>
          <h2 id="ev-cal-title" class="card-h mt-2"><span>{% icon "calendar-days", "size-5" %}</span>{{ "committee.events.cal_title" | t(lang, { n: cal.n }) }}</h2>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn-secondary btn-sm ev-cal-toggle" data-js-only data-ev-cal-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="ev-cal-body" data-show="{{ 'evlist.cal_show' | t(lang) }}" data-hide="{{ 'evlist.cal_hide' | t(lang) }}">{% icon "chevron-down", "size-4" %}<span data-ev-cal-label>{{ "evlist.cal_show" | t(lang) }}</span></button>
      </div>
      <div id="ev-cal-body" class="ev-cal-body">
      <p class="cm-cal-cap" data-cm-cal-cap="{{ cal.captionFrom }}">{{ cal.caption }}</p>
      <table class="cm-cal" aria-labelledby="ev-cal-title">
        <thead>
          <tr>{% for wd in cal.weekdays %}<th scope="col"><span class="cm-cal-wd" aria-hidden="true">{{ wd.short }}</span><span class="cm-cal-wd2" aria-hidden="true">{{ wd.tiny }}</span><span class="sr-only">{{ wd.long }}</span></th>{% endfor %}</tr>
        </thead>
        {#- (whitespace control throughout: 56 cells and a list per day add up) -#}
        <tbody data-cm-max="{{ cal.n }}">
          {%- for wk in cal.weeks -%}
          <tr data-cm-expire="{{ wk.endIso }}"{% if wk.hidden %} class="hidden"{% endif %}>
            {%- for d in wk.days -%}
            <td class="cm-cal-d{{ ' is-today' if d.today }}{{ ' is-past' if d.past }}{{ ' is-selected' if d.ymd == cal.panel }}" data-cm-day="{{ d.ymd }}"{% if d.today %} aria-current="date"{% endif %}>
              {%- if d.events | length -%}
              <a class="cm-cal-link"{% if not d.past %} href="#{{ d.first }}"{% endif %} data-cm-cal-day="{{ d.ymd }}">{% if d.mon %}<span class="cm-cal-mon" aria-hidden="true">{{ d.mon }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="cm-cal-n" aria-hidden="true">{{ d.day }}</span><span class="sr-only">{{ d.sr }}</span><span class="cm-cal-dots" aria-hidden="true">{% for e in d.dots %}<span class="cm-cal-dot ev-tone-{{ e.tone }}{{ ' is-weekly' if e.weekly }}"></span>{% endfor %}{% if d.more %}<span class="cm-cal-more">+{{ d.more }}</span>{% endif %}</span></a>
              {%- else -%}
              <span class="cm-cal-day">{% if d.mon %}<span class="cm-cal-mon">{{ d.mon }}</span>{% endif %}{{ d.day }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </td>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tr>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="cm-cal-panels" aria-live="polite" data-cm-cal-panels data-today="{{ 'common.today' | t(lang) }}" data-next="{{ 'committee.events.cal_next_up' | t(lang) }}">
        {%- for wk in cal.weeks %}{% for d in wk.days %}{% if d.events | length -%}
        <div class="cm-cal-panel" data-cm-cal-panel="{{ d.ymd }}"{% if d.ymd != cal.panel %} hidden{% endif %}>
          <h3 class="cm-cal-ph"><span class="cm-cal-tag" data-cm-cal-tag>{% if d.ymd == cal.panel %}{{ ("common.today" if cal.panelToday else "committee.events.cal_next_up") | t(lang) }}{% endif %}</span> {{ d.label }}</h3>
          <ul class="cm-cal-list" role="list">
            {%- for e in d.events -%}
            <li data-cm-cal-end="{{ e.endIso }}"><span class="cm-cal-dot ev-tone-{{ e.tone }}{{ ' is-weekly' if e.weekly }}"></span><span>{% if e.time %}<span class="cm-cal-time">{{ e.time }}</span> {% endif %}<a class="cm-cal-ev" href="#{{ e.anchor }}">{{ e.title }}</a>{% if e.weekly %} <span class="cm-cal-wk">· {{ "committee.events.badge_weekly" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}</span></li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <ul class="cm-cal-key" role="list" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.legend' | t(lang) }}">
        {%- for k in cal.kinds %}
        <li><span class="cm-cal-dot ev-tone-{{ k.tone }}"></span>{{ k.label }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- if cal.weekly %}
        <li><span class="cm-cal-dot is-weekly"></span>{{ "committee.events.badge_weekly" | t(lang) }}</li>
        {%- endif %}
      </ul>
      <p class="cm-cal-help">{{ "committee.events.cal_help" | t(lang) }}</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</aside>
{% endif %}

{#- (round 38b) The list's component: cmEvents (src/assets/js/committee.js) — or, when committee.js did not load but
    Alpine did (a download that failed or was blocked, a saved copy without it), a stand-in that shows what the page
    without JavaScript shows: every card (show) and every month (monthVisible; `more`: the fold open, and its
    first-paint rule let go — .cm-ev-ready). The list was blank then: each card's x-show asked a cmEvents that was not
    there. The filters need cmEvents, so the stand-in hides them (#ev-filters); its other names (f, group, active,
    the counts …) answer what the filters, "Showing N events" and the empty states ask, so no expression of the list
    fails. tests/browser/test_events_list_browser.py (Fallback) blocks committee.js; tests/test_r30_events_list.py runs
    the stand-in on folded months. -#}
{%- set evStandIn = "{ f: {}, group: '', active: false, moreOpen: false, more: true, anyMonth: true, show() { return true }, monthVisible() { return true }, kindCount() { return '' }, groupCount() { return '' }, countText() { return '' }, moreText() { return '' }, init() { document.documentElement.classList.add('cm-ev-ready'); (this.$el.querySelector('#ev-filters') || {}).hidden = true } }" %}
{#- (data-cm-note-timed / -day: the words of the cards' "Add to calendar" note, once — evm.calMenu) -#}
<section class="ev-main min-w-0" x-data="typeof cmEvents == 'function' ? cmEvents() : {{ evStandIn }}" data-count-label="{{ 'committee.events.showing' | t(lang) }}" data-count-label-one="{{ 'committee.events.showing_one' | t(lang) }}" data-cm-note-timed="{{ 'committee.cal.reminder_timed' | t(lang) }}" data-cm-note-day="{{ 'committee.cal.reminder_day' | t(lang) }}" aria-labelledby="ev-upcoming-title">
  {{ ui.sectionHead("committee.events.upcoming" | t(lang), "committee.events.list_sub" | t(lang), "", "", "calendar-days", { eyebrow: "committee.events.list_eyebrow" | t(lang), tone: "text-vine", id: "ev-upcoming-title", lang: lang }) }}

  {#- ---------- The filters (JavaScript only: without it every card shows) — cmEvents (src/assets/js/committee.js):
       the kind as chips (each with its count under the menus picked) and, just before "GV & LV calendars", "NETA 65
       events" (the page's old chip, back in round 38: our events and the committee meeting — data-group~="neta";
       netaChip) — the chips one choice, as the old ones were (round 38b: picking one lets the other go) —, then the
       language, in person / online, the city and the district (only when an event names one) as menus, and "Clear
       filters". Every card of the page carries its facets (evFacets: data-kind, data-lang, data-mode, data-city,
       data-district) — the one-off events, the cancelled ones, the series' cards and the weekly meetings alike. The
       filters picked are kept in the address (?kind=…&lang=…, ?filter=neta), so a filtered view can be shared;
       ?filter=committee / ?filter=calendar / ?filter=neta (the page's old chips) still work — the GV & LV calendars'
       chip shows what its old one did (La Viña's monthly workshop and the weekly open meetings are of that kind too:
       event-list.js facetsOf). Then the months as jump chips (only those with something showing), "Every month" and
       "Every week", and the colour key. ---------- -#}
  {#- "NETA 65 events": its count the build's, then the browser's (groupCount, with the menus picked) -#}
  {%- macro netaChip(g) %}{% if g %}<button type="button" class="chip" data-ev-group="neta" @click="setGroup('neta')" :aria-pressed="(group === 'neta').toString()" aria-pressed="false">{% icon "map-pin", "size-4" %} {{ "evlist.group.neta" | t(lang) }} <span class="cm-chip-count" x-text="groupCount('neta')">{{ g.n }}</span></button>{% endif %}{% endmacro -%}
  {%- set fold = L.oneOff | cmEventsFold -%}
  <div class="mb-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-3">
    <div id="ev-filters" class="ev-filters" data-js-only role="group" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.filter_aria' | t(lang) }}">
      <div class="chip-row" role="group" aria-label="{{ 'evlist.kind_aria' | t(lang) }}">
        <button type="button" class="chip" data-ev-kind="" @click="all()" :aria-pressed="(!f.kind && !group).toString()" aria-pressed="true">{% icon "layout-grid", "size-4" %} {{ "common.all" | t(lang) }}</button>
        {%- set netaG = L.facets.groups | first %}
        {%- for k in L.facets.kinds %}
        {%- if k.key == "calendar" %}
        {{ netaChip(netaG) }}
        {%- endif %}
        <button type="button" class="chip" data-ev-kind="{{ k.key }}" @click="setKind('{{ k.key }}')" :aria-pressed="(f.kind === '{{ k.key }}').toString()" aria-pressed="false">{{ ("evlist.kind." + k.key) | t(lang) }} <span class="cm-chip-count" x-text="kindCount('{{ k.key }}')">{{ k.n }}</span></button>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- if not (L.facets.kinds | where("key", "calendar") | length) %}
        {{ netaChip(netaG) }}
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {#- (below 640px the menus fold behind "More filters" — open by themselves when the address picks one of them;
          "Clear filters" beside it, from 640px after the menus) -#}
      <div class="ev-filter-tools">
        <button type="button" class="btn-ghost btn-sm ev-more-filters" @click="moreOpen = !moreOpen" :aria-expanded="moreOpen.toString()" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="ev-filter-row">{% icon "sliders-horizontal", "size-4" %} {{ "evlist.more_filters" | t(lang) }}</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-ghost btn-sm ev-clear" x-show="active" x-cloak @click="clear()">{% icon "x", "size-4" %} {{ "evlist.clear" | t(lang) }}</button>
      </div>
      <div id="ev-filter-row" class="ev-filter-row" :class="moreOpen && 'is-open'">
        {%- if L.facets.langs | length > 1 %}
        <label class="ev-select"><span class="ev-select-l">{{ "evlist.lang_label" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <select class="input" data-ev-facet="lang" x-model="f.lang" @change="changed()">
            <option value="">{{ "evlist.lang.any" | t(lang) }}</option>
            {%- for v in L.facets.langs %}<option value="{{ v }}">{{ ("evlist.lang." + v) | t(lang) }}</option>{% endfor %}
          </select></label>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if L.facets.modes | length > 1 %}
        <label class="ev-select"><span class="ev-select-l">{{ "evlist.mode_label" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <select class="input" data-ev-facet="mode" x-model="f.mode" @change="changed()">
            <option value="">{{ "evlist.mode.any" | t(lang) }}</option>
            {%- for v in L.facets.modes %}<option value="{{ v }}">{{ ("evlist.mode." + v) | t(lang) }}</option>{% endfor %}
          </select></label>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if L.facets.cities | length > 1 %}
        <label class="ev-select"><span class="ev-select-l">{{ "evlist.city_label" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <select class="input" data-ev-facet="city" x-model="f.city" @change="changed()">
            <option value="">{{ "evlist.city_any" | t(lang) }}</option>
            {%- for c in L.facets.cities %}<option value="{{ c.slug }}">{{ c.name }}</option>{% endfor %}
          </select></label>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if L.facets.districts | length %}
        <label class="ev-select"><span class="ev-select-l">{{ "evlist.district_label" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <select class="input" data-ev-facet="district" x-model="f.district" @change="changed()">
            <option value="">{{ "evlist.district_any" | t(lang) }}</option>
            {%- for d in L.facets.districts %}<option value="{{ d.d }}">{{ "evlist.district" | t(lang, { n: d.d }) }}</option>{% endfor %}
          </select></label>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- set months = L.oneOff | groupBy("monthKey") %}
    {% if months | length or L.series | length or gm or wos | length %}
    {#- (the whole row goes while none of its chips shows — the filters picked show nothing: anyMonth) #}
    <nav class="flex min-w-0 max-w-full items-center gap-2.5" x-show="anyMonth" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.months_aria' | t(lang) }}">
      <span class="shrink-0 text-faint" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "calendar-range", "size-4" %}</span>
      <ul class="chip-row min-w-0" role="list">
        {%- for grp in months %}
        <li x-show="monthVisible($refs['m{{ grp.key }}']) && (more || !$el.hasAttribute('data-cm-more'))"{% if fold and grp.key >= fold.from %} data-cm-more data-dflt-hidden{% endif %}><a class="chip" href="#month-{{ grp.key }}">{{ grp.items[0].monthShort }}</a></li>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- if L.series | length or gm %}<li x-show="monthVisible($refs.series)"><a class="chip" href="#ev-pinned-title">{% icon "repeat", "size-4" %} {{ "evlist.series_title" | t(lang) }}</a></li>{% endif %}
        {%- if wos | length %}<li x-show="monthVisible($refs.weekly)"><a class="chip" href="#ev-weekly-title">{% icon "repeat", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.events.badge_weekly" | t(lang) }}</a></li>{% endif %}
      </ul>
    </nav>
    {% endif %}
    {#- the colour key: only the kinds on this page (committee meeting · Grapevine · La Viña · booth · Area event ·
        the grey one), each card's badge says its kind in words too — the series' cards and the "every week" cards
        below (#ev-weekly: Grapevine's and La Viña's colours) count as well. The grey kind is "NETA 65" when every grey
        card is one of ours (its badge says so: kindBadge — today the Grapevine Meeting), else "Other events". -#}
    {%- set toneSrc = upcoming.concat([gm.next] if gm else []) -%}
    {%- for w in wos %}{% set _n = toneSrc.push({ host: "lv" if w.isLv else "gv" }) %}{% endfor -%}
    {%- set kinds = toneSrc | eventToneSet %}
    {%- set greyOthers = [] -%}
    {%- for ev in toneSrc %}{% if ev.group != "neta" and (ev | eventTone) == "other" and greyOthers.push(ev) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    {% if kinds | length > 1 %}
    <div class="ev-legend">
      <span class="ev-legend-label" id="ev-legend-label">{{ "committee.events.legend" | t(lang) }}</span>
      <ul class="ev-legend-list" role="list" aria-labelledby="ev-legend-label">
        {%- for k in kinds %}
        <li class="ev-tone-{{ k }}"><span class="ev-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ ("committee.events.kind." + ("neta" if (k == "other" and not greyOthers.length) else k)) | t(lang) }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" x-text="countText()"></p>

  {#- ---------- The one-off events, grouped by month ----------
      Every event to come that is not a date of a monthly series nor a committee meeting, a card each (evList oneOff),
      and the cancelled ones until their day is over. A folded month (fold: a year after the open ones) carries
      data-cm-more + data-dflt-hidden and shows once "Show {range} dates (n)" is pressed (cmEvents `more`); its heading
      takes the keyboard then (tabindex="-1"). That button comes right after the last open month: data-js-only, shown
      while a folded card the filters pick is hidden, with their count (moreCount; the build writes the "All" count). -#}
  {% for grp in months %}
  {%- set folded = fold and grp.key >= fold.from %}
  {% if folded and grp.key == fold.keys[0] %}
  <div class="cm-ev-more" data-js-only x-show="!more && moreCount">
    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary" @click="showMore()">{% icon "chevron-down", "size-4" %} <span data-label="{{ 'committee.events.show_more' | t(lang, { range: fold.range }) }}" x-text="moreText($el)">{{ "committee.events.show_more" | t(lang, { range: fold.range, n: fold.n }) }}</span></button>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <section class="cm-month" data-cm-month x-ref="m{{ grp.key }}" x-show="monthVisible($el) && (more || !$el.hasAttribute('data-cm-more'))"{% if folded %} data-cm-more data-dflt-hidden{% endif %} aria-labelledby="month-{{ grp.key }}">
    <h2 id="month-{{ grp.key }}" class="cm-month-title"{% if folded %} tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>{{ grp.items[0].monthLabel }}</h2>
    <ol class="grid gap-4">
      {% for ev in grp.items %}
      {%- set kind = ev | eventTone %}
      {%- if ev.cancelled %}
      {#- A cancelled event, until its day is over (db.events.cancelled — content/events `cancelled: true`; the site
          search lists it the same way): its card struck through, "Cancelled", the day and place it had, its title and
          "See the notice" to its notice page (/events/<anchor>/: src/pages/event-share-cancelled.njk) — no calendar
          menu, no flyer, no way to join: nothing invites anyone to come. Never counted ("Showing N events") -#}
      <li id="{{ ev.anchor }}" data-group="{{ ev.group }}" data-ev-cancelled data-cm-expire="{{ ev.expireIso }}"{{ ev | evFacets(site) | safe }} x-show="show($el)">
        <article class="card cm-event ev-accent ev-tone-{{ kind }} ev-cancelled" x-ignore>
          <div class="cm-date-tile{{ ' cm-tile-range' if ev.tile.range }} max-sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="cm-tile-mon">{{ ev.tile.mon }}</span>
            <span class="cm-tile-day">{{ ev.tile.day }}</span>
            <span class="cm-tile-wd">{{ ev.tile.wd }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <p class="cm-date-strip mb-2.5 sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "calendar", "size-3.5" %}<span>{{ ev.tile.wd }} · {{ ev.tile.mon }} {{ ev.tile.day }}</span></p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
              <span class="badge ev-badge-cancelled">{% icon "calendar-x", "size-3" %} {{ "evcancel.ics_prefix" | t(lang) }}</span>
              {{ evm.kindBadge(ev, kind) }}
            </div>
            <h3 class="h-card mt-2 text-lg sm:text-xl"><a href="{{ ev.noticePath }}" class="-my-3 inline-block py-3 hover:text-gv"><s>{{ ev.title }}</s><span class="sr-only"> — {{ "evcancel.ics_prefix" | t(lang) }}</span></a></h3>
            <p class="sr-only">{{ ev.dateLabel }}</p>
            <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
              {% if ev.multiDay %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "calendar-range", "size-4 text-faint" %} <s>{{ ev.rangeLabel }}</s></li>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.timeLabel %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "clock-3", "size-4 text-faint" %} <s>{{ ev.timeLabel }}</s></li>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.location %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "map-pin", "size-4 text-faint" %} <s>{{ ev.location }}</s></li>{% endif %}
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-ink">{{ ev.cancelledNote or ("evcancel.banner" | t(lang)) }}</p>
            <div class="cm-ev-actions"><div class="cm-ev-btns"><a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ ev.noticePath }}">{% icon "info", "size-4" %} {{ "evlist.notice" | t(lang) }}</a></div></div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </li>
      {%- else %}
      {#- Share: the event's own page, /events/<anchor>/ (eleventy/event-pages.js eventPagePlan — src/pages/
          event-share-leaf.njk while it is to come, event-share-date.njk for an outside calendar's event), whose link
          preview shows its title, day and flyer (the card's title links to it below) -#}
      {%- set shareUrl = ("/events/" + ev.anchor + "/") | lurl(lang) | siteUrl(site) %}
      {#- data-group: who it is from (committee · neta · calendar); evFacets: its filters (see the filter bar above).
          x-ignore: Alpine never walks into a card. A card holds NO Alpine directive (x-…, @…, :…) — its x-show is on
          the <li> — and must not: one put inside would silently do nothing (tests/test_r33_committee.py checks the
          built page). Its menus, Share and flyer buttons are plain HTML and committee.js / app.js. Its old anchors
          ("ev-flyer-…", before it had a readable address: evOldAnchors) are empty spans on it, so an old link lands on
          it too. -#}
      <li id="{{ ev.anchor }}" data-group="{{ ev.group }}" data-cm-expire="{{ ev.expireIso }}"{{ ev | evFacets(site) | safe }} x-show="show($el)">
        <article class="card cm-event ev-accent ev-tone-{{ kind }}" x-ignore>
          {%- for a in ev.item | evOldAnchors %}<span id="{{ a }}" class="sr-only"></span>{% endfor %}
          {#- the date: a tile column from 640px; on a phone a strip above the title (+ Share as an icon) -#}
          <div class="cm-date-tile{{ ' cm-tile-range' if ev.tile.range }} max-sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="cm-tile-mon">{{ ev.tile.mon }}</span>
            <span class="cm-tile-day">{{ ev.tile.day }}</span>
            <span class="cm-tile-wd">{{ ev.tile.wd }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <div class="mb-2.5 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 sm:hidden">
              <p class="cm-date-strip" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "calendar", "size-3.5" %}<span>{{ ev.tile.wd }} · {{ ev.tile.mon }} {{ ev.tile.day }}</span></p>
              <button type="button" class="btn-ghost -my-1 -mr-2 size-11 shrink-0 p-0" data-js-only data-share="{{ shareUrl }}" data-share-title="{{ ev.title }}" data-share-text="{{ ev.shareWhen }}" aria-label="{{ 'common.share' | t(lang) }}: {{ ev.title }}">{% icon "share-2", "size-4" %}</button>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
              {{ evm.kindBadge(ev, kind) }}
              {% if ev.tentative %}{{ ui.tentativeBadge(lang) }}{% endif %}
              {% if ev.isNew %}<span class="badge-new">{{ "common.new" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}
              {% if not ev.ownWords %}{{ ui.langPill(ev.item, lang) }}{% endif %}
            </div>
            {#- the title: a link to the event's own page (eleventy/filters/event-links.js evHref), else — an event the
                build writes no page for — to its link (an outside page) when that is not its flyer -#}
            {%- set ownPage = ev | evHref(lang, db, site, "page") -%}
            <h3 class="h-card mt-2 text-lg sm:text-xl">
              {%- if ev.link and ev.link != (ev.flyer.view if ev.flyer else "") and not ownPage -%}
              <a href="{{ ev.link }}" class="-my-3 inline-block py-3 hover:text-gv"{% if ev.linkExternal %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ ev.title }}</a>
              {%- elif ownPage -%}
              <a href="{{ ownPage }}" class="-my-3 inline-block py-3 hover:text-gv">{{ ev.title }}</a>
              {%- else -%}{{ ev.title }}{%- endif -%}
            </h3>
            {#- the tile is hidden from screen readers: the date is read here (a range is in the list below) -#}
            {% if not ev.multiDay %}<p class="sr-only">{{ ev.dateLabel }}</p>{% endif %}
            <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
              {#- Several days (an Area assembly): the date range; the tile shows it too -#}
              {% if ev.multiDay %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-medium text-ink">{% icon "calendar-range", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.rangeLabel }}</li>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.timeLabel %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "clock-3", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.timeLabel }}</li>{% endif %}
              {#- A place not known yet ("Venue to be announced"): plain italic text, no map pin -#}
              {% if ev.location and ev.locationTba %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 italic">{% icon "hourglass", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.location }}</li>
              {% elif ev.location %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "map-pin", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.location }}</li>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.isOnline %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ("committee.events.online_on" | t(lang, { platform: ev.platform })) if ev.platform else ("committee.events.online" | t(lang)) }}</li>{% endif %}
              {#- the meeting ID or code to type into the meeting app — inline-block: with larger text the number moves to
                  the next line in one piece; data-nosnippet: never quoted by search engines -#}
              {% if ev.meetingId %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "hash", "size-4 text-faint" %} <span>{{ ev.meetingIdKey | t(lang) }} <span class="inline-block whitespace-nowrap font-mono font-medium text-ink" translate="no" data-nosnippet>{{ ev.meetingId }}</span></span></li>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.contact %}<li class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "mail", "size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <a class="link tap-link min-w-0 break-words" href="mailto:{{ ev.contact }}" translate="no"><span class="sr-only">{{ "committee.events.contact" | t(lang) }}: </span>{{ ev.contact | replace("@", "@<wbr>") | safe }}</a></li>{% endif %}
              {#- a content/events file's `district:` -#}
              {% if ev.facets.district %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "map", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ "evlist.district" | t(lang, { n: ev.facets.district }) }}</li>{% endif %}
            </ul>
            {%- set foreign = not ev.ownWords and ev.item.lang and ev.item.lang != lang and ev.item.lang != "und" and not (ev.item | machineFor(lang)) -%}
            {#- the summary, three lines of it (its whole description is on its own page): a meeting ID, Meet code,
                passcode or meeting address in it is never quoted by search engines (cmNoSnippet) -#}
            {% if ev.summary %}
            <p class="mt-2.5 line-clamp-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted"{% if foreign %} lang="{{ ev.item.lang }}"{% endif %}>{{ ev.summary | excerpt(280) | escape | cmNoSnippet | safe }}</p>
            {% endif %}
            {% if ev.item | machineFor(lang) %}<p class="mt-1.5">{{ ui.autoNote(ev.item, lang) }}</p>{% endif %}
            {#- phones: a two-column grid of equal buttons (an odd last one spans both); from 640px one row, with Share
                at its end (committee.css .cm-ev-actions). Its outside page, when it is not its flyer: "Organizer's
                page ↗" (organizerButton) — the title goes to its own page here. -#}
            <div class="cm-ev-actions">
              <div class="cm-ev-btns">
              {% if ev.online %}
              <a class="btn-primary btn-sm" href="{{ ev.online }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "globe", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.join_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "committee.events.join_online" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>
              {% endif %}
              {{ evm.calMenu(ev) }}
              {{ ui.flyerButton(ev.flyer, ev.title, lang) }}
              {% if ev.link and ev.linkExternal and (not ev.flyer or (ownPage and ev.link != ev.flyer.view)) %}{{ organizerButton(ev) }}{% endif %}
              </div>
              <button type="button" class="btn-ghost btn-sm max-xl:px-2.5 max-sm:hidden" data-js-only data-share="{{ shareUrl }}" data-share-title="{{ ev.title }}" data-share-text="{{ ev.shareWhen }}">{% icon "share-2", "size-4" %}<span class="max-xl:sr-only">{{ "common.share" | t(lang) }}</span></button>
            </div>
          </div>
          {#- The flyer on the side (from 640px; on a phone the "View flyer" button above is the way to it) -#}
          {{ ui.flyerThumb(ev.flyer, ev.title, lang) }}
        </article>
      </li>
      {%- endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  {#- nothing the filters picked (cmEvents: no card shows, nor one folded behind "Show 2028 dates": moreCount — that
      button says how many are there) — "Clear filters" brings every card back -#}
  <div class="mt-2" data-js-only x-show="active && !visibleCount && !moreCount" x-cloak>
    <div class="empty-state">
      <span class="mx-auto mb-3 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-surface-2 text-faint">{% icon "search-x", "size-6" %}</span>
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink">{{ "evlist.none_title" | t(lang) }}</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-1 max-w-md text-sm">{{ "evlist.none_text" | t(lang) }}</p>
      <button type="button" class="btn-secondary btn-sm mt-4" @click="clear()">{{ "evlist.clear" | t(lang) }}</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- ---------- Every month: ONE card per monthly series (evList series) ----------
      The committee meeting first — the dark card, the page's FIRST .cm-pinned (tests read its settings) —, then the
      monthly series in the order of their next date: the Grapevine Meeting (#ev-next-gvm, built like a weekly open
      meeting's card) and the others (#ev-series-<key>). Each a card of the list ([data-group], its facets, x-show),
      shown or hidden by the filters like any other, counted once. The committee meeting's and the Grapevine Meeting's
      cards roll on in the browser (cmMeeting: the next date once one is over, "Live now" during it, the visitor's own
      time); a series' card lists its next three dates — the rest wait hidden and take their place as each is over
      (expire(): data-cm-max) — each a link to its date's own page, then what changed about its dates and "See all
      dates". Every date's anchor is on its series' card. The Grapevine Meeting's card is worked out from the settings
      (gm), so it shows before the data sync lists its dates too — then after the others, with no dates of its own. -#}
  {%- set seriesCards = L.series.slice() -%}
  {%- if gm and not (L.series | where("key", "grapevine-meeting") | length) %}{% set _gm = seriesCards.push({ key: "grapevine-meeting", committee: false, next: gm.next, dates: [], notes: [], href: "", expireIso: gm.next.expireIso }) %}{% endif -%}
  {#- (round 38) The months that have only dates of a monthly series or committee meetings (no one-off event, so no
      month of their own above) keep their old anchors here — #month-2028-03, from the page's month chips before the
      list's redesign: a link to one lands on "Every month" (committee.js go: its heading) -#}
  {%- set ownMonths = [] -%}{%- for grp in months %}{% set _m = ownMonths.push(grp.key) %}{% endfor -%}
  {%- set seriesMonths = [] -%}
  {%- for ev in upcoming %}{% if ev.monthKey and ev.monthKey not in ownMonths and ev.monthKey not in seriesMonths %}{% set _m = seriesMonths.push(ev.monthKey) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
  {% if seriesCards | length %}
  <section id="ev-pinned" class="ev-series-sec" x-ref="series" x-show="monthVisible($el)" aria-labelledby="ev-pinned-title">
    {% if seriesMonths | length %}<div data-ev-anchors>{% for k in seriesMonths %}<span id="month-{{ k }}"></span>{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
    <h2 id="ev-pinned-title" class="cm-month-title">{% icon "repeat", "size-5 shrink-0 text-grape" %}{{ "evlist.series_title" | t(lang) }}</h2>
    <p class="measure -mt-1.5 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ "evlist.series_text" | t(lang) }}</p>
    <ul class="grid gap-4" role="list">
  {%- for s in seriesCards %}
  {%- if s.committee and next %}
  {#- (1) the next committee meeting: the dark card. The guest speakers to come, each with that meeting's calendar
      text: the card shows the speaker of the date it shows — none on a date without one —, also once it rolls on in
      the browser (committee.js cmSpeakers) -#}
  {%- set spk = site | cmSpeakers(lang) -%}
  {%- set cfg = { rule: m | cmRuleObj, start: next.startIso, end: next.endIso, title: next.title, description: next.calDescription, location: next.calLocation, url: ('/meetings/#committee-meeting' | lurl(lang) | siteUrl(site)), speakers: spk.list, plain: spk.plain, i18n: { join: "committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, pf), soon: "committee.meeting.join_soon" | t(lang), live: "committee.meeting.join_live" | t(lang), yourTime: "committee.meeting.your_time" | t(lang), speaker: "committee.meeting.speaker" | t(lang) } } -%}
  <li data-group="committee neta" data-cm-expire="{{ s.expireIso }}"{{ s.next | evFacets(site) | safe }}{% if s.datesHref %} data-ev-dates="{{ s.datesHref | url }}"{% endif %} x-show="show($el)">
  {{ dateAnchors(s) }}
  <article class="cm-pinned @container" x-data="cmMeeting({{ cfg | json }})" aria-labelledby="ev-next-title">
    <div class="cm-pinned-grid">
      <div class="cm-date-tile cm-tone-light" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="cm-tile-mon" x-text="tile.mon">{{ next.tile.mon }}</span>
        <span class="cm-tile-day" x-text="tile.day">{{ next.tile.day }}</span>
        <span class="cm-tile-wd" x-text="tile.wd">{{ next.tile.wd }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-white/75">
          {% icon "repeat", "size-3.5" %}
          <span x-show="phase === 'upcoming'">{{ "committee.events.pinned_next" | t(lang) }}</span>
          {#- ("Live now": no text in the page until it is true — its words in data-label, Alpine writes them) -#}
          <span x-show="phase !== 'upcoming'" x-cloak class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span class="cm-live-dot"></span><span data-label="{{ 'committee.meeting.live_now' | t(lang) }}" x-text="$el.dataset.label"></span></span>
        </p>
        <h3 id="ev-next-title" class="mt-1.5 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight text-white">{{ next.title }}</h3>
        <p class="mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-white/80">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} <span x-text="dateLabel">{{ next.dateLabel }}</span></span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "clock-3", "size-4" %} <span x-text="timeLabel">{{ next.timeLabel }}</span></span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ pf.platform }}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-white/80">{% icon "repeat", "size-4" %} {{ m | cmRule(lang) }}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-white/65" x-show="localLabel" x-text="localLabel" x-cloak></p>
        {% if spk.list | length %}
        <p class="mt-2 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm text-white/85" x-show="speaker"{% if not next.speaker %} x-cloak{% endif %}>
          {% icon "mic", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0" %}
          <span class="min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold text-white" x-text="speakerLine">{{ ("committee.meeting.speaker" | t(lang, { name: next.speaker.name })) if next.speaker }}</span><span x-show="speaker && speaker.topic"> — “<span x-text="speaker ? speaker.topic : ''">{{ next.speaker.topic if next.speaker }}</span>”</span></span>
        </p>
        {% endif %}
        {{ seriesNotes(s, true) }}
      </div>
      <div class="cm-pinned-actions">
        <a href="{{ next.online or m.online_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-light btn-sm" :class="phase !== 'upcoming' && 'cm-join-live'">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} <span x-text="joinText">{{ "committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, pf) }}</span></a>
        {#- (in the page the brief Google / Outlook links, as on the cards — evm.calMenu; Alpine's :href puts the
            full ones in, with the description of the date it shows) -#}
        <details class="cm-menu">
          <summary class="btn-on-dark btn-sm">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} {{ "common.add_to_calendar" | t(lang) }}</summary>
          <div class="cm-menu-panel cm-menu-right">
            <a :href="gcal" href="{{ next.gcalBrief }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Google Calendar</a>
            <a :href="outlook" href="{{ next.outlookBrief }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Outlook.com</a>
            <button type="button" @click="downloadIcs()" data-cm-js>{% icon "download", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.cal.ics_file" | t(lang) }}</button>
            <p class="cm-menu-note" data-cm-js>{{ "committee.cal.reminder_timed" | t(lang) }}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        {#- (round 38) every date to come, each with its own Add to calendar, flyer and Share: its dates page -#}
        {% if s.datesHref %}<a href="{{ s.datesHref }}" class="btn-on-dark btn-sm">{% icon "calendar-range", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "evpage.sec.all_dates" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "evlist.series_all" | t(lang) }}</span></a>{% endif %}
        <a href="{{ s.href }}" class="btn-on-dark btn-sm">{% icon "info", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.events.meeting_details" | t(lang) }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  </li>
  {%- elif s.key == "grapevine-meeting" and gm %}
  {#- (2) the Grapevine Meeting: site | cmSeriesNext("grapevine-meeting") (worked out from the settings, so it is
      right before the data sync lists it). Built like a weekly open meeting's card (#ev-weekly below) in its own grey
      (ev-tone-other: ours, never Grapevine's colour — its badge says NETA 65, with the camera: online only): "Every
      month", "In English" unless its title says so, the title (its series' page), the rule and time, "Online on
      Google Meet", then the next date — cmMeeting (the /meetings/#grapevine-meeting countdown's settings, gmCfg: the
      UID /events.ics gives each date, so adding it twice keeps one entry; `first`: "First meeting:" on the series'
      first date) rolls it on, says "Live now" during the meeting and adds the visitor's own time. Join on Google Meet,
      See all dates (its series' page), Add to calendar and its flyer. -#}
  {%- set gmPf = { platform: gm.join.platform } -%}
  {%- set gmJoin = ("committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, gmPf)) if gm.join.platform else ("committee.events.join_online" | t(lang)) -%}
  {%- set gmCfg = {
    rule: gm.rule, start: gm.next.startIso, end: gm.next.endIso, title: gm.next.title, description: gm.next.calDescription,
    location: gm.next.calLocation, url: gm.next.detailsUrl, uid: gm.uidPrefix, file: "grapevine-meeting-", first: gm.starts,
    i18n: { join: gmJoin, soon: "committee.meeting.join_soon" | t(lang), live: "committee.meeting.join_live" | t(lang), yourTime: "committee.meeting.your_time" | t(lang) }
  } -%}
  {%- set gmFirst = gm.next.startYmd == gm.starts -%}
  <li data-group="{{ s.next.group }}" data-cm-expire="{{ s.expireIso }}"{{ s.next | evFacets(site) | safe }} x-show="show($el)">
  {{ dateAnchors(s) }}
  <article id="ev-next-gvm" class="card ev-accent ev-tone-other cm-event" x-data="cmMeeting({{ gmCfg | json }})" aria-labelledby="ev-next-gvm-title">
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
        {{ evm.kindBadge(gm.next, "other") }}
        <span class="badge-muted">{% icon "repeat", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.events.badge_recurring" | t(lang) }}</span>
        {% if not gm.saysLang %}<span class="badge-muted">{% icon "languages", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.weekly.lang_en" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <h3 id="ev-next-gvm-title" class="h-card mt-2 text-lg sm:text-xl">{% if s.href %}<a href="{{ s.href }}" class="-my-3 inline-block py-3 hover:text-gv">{{ gm.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ gm.title }}{% endif %}</h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
        <li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "repeat", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{{ gm.recurrenceDay }} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {{ gm.time }}</span></li>
        <li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{{ ("committee.events.online_on" | t(lang, gmPf)) if gm.join.platform else ("committee.events.online" | t(lang)) }}</span></li>
        {#- (its meeting code, to type into Google Meet — never quoted by search engines: before the list's redesign the
            card of each of its dates showed it) -#}
        {% if gm.next.meetingId %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "hash", "size-4 text-faint" %} <span>{{ gm.next.meetingIdKey | t(lang) }} <span class="inline-block whitespace-nowrap font-mono font-medium text-ink" translate="no" data-nosnippet>{{ gm.next.meetingId }}</span></span></li>{% endif %}
      </ul>
      {#- Its label: "Live now" during the meeting, else "First meeting:" on the series' first date, else "Next
          meeting:". A label that is not true when the page is built is no text in it — its words wait in data-label
          and Alpine writes them; the one true at the build is written out too, so the page reads right without
          JavaScript. -#}
      {%- set gmLabels = { live: "committee.meeting.live_now" | t(lang), first: "committee.events.first_meeting" | t(lang), next: "committee.weekly.next" | t(lang) } -%}
      <p class="mt-2.5 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted">
        {% icon "calendar", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}
        <span class="min-w-0">
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink" x-show="phase === 'live'" x-cloak data-label="{{ gmLabels.live }}" x-text="$el.dataset.label"></span>
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink" x-show="phase !== 'live' && isFirst"{% if not gmFirst %} x-cloak{% endif %} data-label="{{ gmLabels.first }}" x-text="$el.dataset.label">{{ gmLabels.first if gmFirst }}</span>
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink" x-show="phase !== 'live' && !isFirst"{% if gmFirst %} x-cloak{% endif %} data-label="{{ gmLabels.next }}" x-text="$el.dataset.label">{{ gmLabels.next if not gmFirst }}</span>
          <span x-text="dateLabel">{{ gm.next.dateLabel }}</span> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <span x-text="timeLabel">{{ gm.next.timeLabel }}</span>
          <span class="block text-xs" x-show="localLabel" x-text="localLabel" x-cloak></span>
        </span>
      </p>
      {{ seriesNotes(s) }}
      <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,9.5rem),1fr))] gap-2 sm:flex sm:flex-wrap">
        {% if gm.join.url %}<a class="btn-primary btn-sm col-span-full" href="{{ gm.join.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" :class="phase !== 'upcoming' && 'cm-join-live'">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} <span x-text="joinText">{{ gmJoin }}</span><span class="sr-only"> — {{ gm.title }} ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>{% endif %}
        {% if s.href %}<a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ s.href }}#evp-all-dates">{% icon "calendar-range", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "evpage.sec.all_dates" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "evlist.series_all" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> — {{ gm.title }}</span></a>{% endif %}
        {#- (the brief links in the page, Alpine's full ones once it runs: as the committee meeting's card above) -#}
        <details class="cm-menu">
          <summary class="btn-secondary btn-sm w-full sm:w-auto">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.cal_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "common.add_to_calendar" | t(lang) }}</span> {% icon "chevron-down", "size-4 opacity-70" %}</summary>
          <div class="cm-menu-panel max-sm:right-0 max-sm:left-auto">
            <a :href="gcal" href="{{ gm.next.gcalBrief }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Google Calendar</a>
            <a :href="outlook" href="{{ gm.next.outlookBrief }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Outlook.com</a>
            <button type="button" @click="downloadIcs()" data-cm-js>{% icon "download", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.cal.ics_file" | t(lang) }}</button>
            <p class="cm-menu-note" data-cm-js>{{ "committee.cal.reminder_timed" | t(lang) }}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ '/meetings/#grapevine-meeting' | lurl(lang) }}">{% icon "info", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.details_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "committee.events.meeting_details" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> — {{ gm.title }}</span></a>
        {{ ui.flyerButton(gm.next.flyer, gm.title, lang, "btn-secondary btn-sm col-span-full") }}
      </div>
    </div>
    {{ ui.flyerThumb(gm.next.flyer, gm.title, lang) }}
  </article>
  </li>
  {%- elif not s.committee %}
  {#- (3) any other monthly series (the CityWide booth, La Viña's workshop …): its kind, "Every month", the title (its
      series' page), how often and its time, where (or online, its meeting ID), its next three dates — each to its
      date's page, the anchor of every date on it —, what changed, then Join online, See all dates, Add to calendar
      (its next date) and the flyer of its next date -#}
  {%- set ev = s.next -%}
  {%- set kind = s.tone -%}
  <li id="ev-series-{{ s.key }}" data-group="{{ ev.group }}" data-cm-expire="{{ s.expireIso }}"{{ ev | evFacets(site) | safe }} x-show="show($el)">
    <article class="card cm-event ev-accent ev-tone-{{ kind }} ev-series" x-ignore>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
          {{ evm.kindBadge(ev, kind) }}
          <span class="badge-muted">{% icon "repeat", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.events.badge_recurring" | t(lang) }}</span>
          {% if not ev.ownWords %}{{ ui.langPill(ev.item, lang) }}{% endif %}
        </div>
        <h3 class="h-card mt-2 text-lg sm:text-xl">{% if s.href %}<a href="{{ s.href }}" class="-my-3 inline-block py-3 hover:text-gv">{{ s.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ s.title }}{% endif %}</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
          {% if s.every %}<li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "repeat", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{{ s.every }}{% if s.time %} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {{ s.time }}{% endif %}</span></li>{% endif %}
          {% if ev.location and ev.locationTba %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 italic">{% icon "hourglass", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.location }}</li>
          {% elif ev.location %}<li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "map-pin", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{{ ev.location }}</span></li>{% endif %}
          {% if ev.isOnline %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ("committee.events.online_on" | t(lang, { platform: ev.platform })) if ev.platform else ("committee.events.online" | t(lang)) }}</li>{% endif %}
          {% if ev.meetingId %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "hash", "size-4 text-faint" %} <span>{{ ev.meetingIdKey | t(lang) }} <span class="inline-block whitespace-nowrap font-mono font-medium text-ink" translate="no" data-nosnippet>{{ ev.meetingId }}</span></span></li>{% endif %}
          {% if ev.contact %}<li class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "mail", "size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <a class="link tap-link min-w-0 break-words" href="mailto:{{ ev.contact }}" translate="no"><span class="sr-only">{{ "committee.events.contact" | t(lang) }}: </span>{{ ev.contact | replace("@", "@<wbr>") | safe }}</a></li>{% endif %}
        </ul>
        {#- (its summary, two lines of it: the whole of it is on its series' page; a meeting ID or code in it never
            quoted by search engines) -#}
        {%- set foreign = not ev.ownWords and ev.item.lang and ev.item.lang != lang and ev.item.lang != "und" and not (ev.item | machineFor(lang)) %}
        {% if ev.summary %}<p class="mt-2.5 line-clamp-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted"{% if foreign %} lang="{{ ev.item.lang }}"{% endif %}>{{ ev.summary | excerpt(200) | escape | cmNoSnippet | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
        <div class="ev-series-next">
          <span class="ev-series-next-l">{{ "evlist.series_next" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <ol class="ev-series-dates" role="list" data-cm-max="{{ s.shown }}">
            {%- for d in s.dates %}
            <li id="{{ d.anchor }}" data-cm-expire="{{ d.expireIso }}"{% if loop.index0 >= s.shown or loop.first %} class="{{ 'hidden' if loop.index0 >= s.shown }}{{ 'is-next' if loop.first }}"{% endif %}>{% if d.href %}<a class="ev-series-date" href="{{ d.href }}">{% else %}<span class="ev-series-date">{% endif %}{{ d.tile.wd }}, {{ d.shortLabel }}{% if d.seriesOf %} <span class="ev-series-moved">{{ "evlist.moved" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}{% for a in d.item | evOldAnchors %}<span id="{{ a }}"></span>{% endfor %}{% if d.href %}</a>{% else %}</span>{% endif %}</li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ol>
        </div>
        {{ seriesNotes(s) }}
        <div class="cm-ev-actions">
          <div class="cm-ev-btns">
          {% if ev.online %}
          <a class="btn-primary btn-sm" href="{{ ev.online }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "globe", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.join_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "committee.events.join_online" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>
          {% endif %}
          {% if s.href %}<a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ s.href }}#evp-all-dates">{% icon "calendar-range", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "evpage.sec.all_dates" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "evlist.series_all" | t(lang) }}</span> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> — {{ s.title }}</span></a>{% endif %}
          {#- (its next date's calendar entry and flyer: gone once that date is over — expire(), data-cm-expire —, so
              the card never offers a date that has passed while its dates roll on in the browser before the next
              build) -#}
          <div class="contents" data-cm-expire="{{ ev.expireIso }}">{{ evm.calMenu(ev) }}{{ ui.flyerButton(ev.flyer, s.title, lang) }}</div>
          {% if ev.link and ev.linkExternal and ev.link != (ev.flyer.view if ev.flyer else "") %}{{ organizerButton(ev) }}{% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="contents" data-cm-expire="{{ ev.expireIso }}">{{ ui.flyerThumb(ev.flyer, s.title, lang) }}</div>
    </article>
  </li>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {#- ---------- Every week: the weekly open meetings ----------
      AA Grapevine's Weekly Open (Wednesdays, in English) and La Viña's Reunión Abierta (Thursdays, in Spanish):
      db.weekly_open.items | cmWeeklyAll, the page language's first — the meetings, dates and calendar files of
      /meetings/#weekly-open, their one home. Not entries of events.json (the /events.ics feeds hold each one as ONE
      entry that repeats every week: committee.js weeklyFeed). Cards of the list like the others: online meetings, in
      their language, online — the filters show or hide them. Each card, in its magazine's colour (ev-tone-gv / -lv,
      kindBadge's "Grapevine" / "La Viña"): "Every week", its language, the title, the day and time (Central · the
      host's), the next date — the /meetings/ cards' data-cm-weekly markup, so committee.js weekly() rolls it on, says
      "Live now" and adds the visitor's own time —, then Join on Zoom (its full Zoom link, with its "?pwd=…"), Meeting
      details (/meetings/#weekly-open: the Zoom ID, passcode, joining by phone, the recordings), Add to calendar (every
      week: Google's link and the .ics file of /meetings/) and View flyer (cmWeeklyFlyer). -#}
  {% if wos | length %}
  <section id="ev-weekly" class="mt-10" x-ref="weekly" x-show="monthVisible($el)" aria-labelledby="ev-weekly-title">
    <h2 id="ev-weekly-title" class="cm-month-title">{{ "committee.weekly.section_title" | t(lang) }}</h2>
    <p class="measure -mt-1.5 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ "committee.events.weekly_text" | t(lang) }}</p>
    <ul class="grid gap-4" role="list">
      {% for w in wos %}
      {%- set key = "lv" if w.isLv else "gv" -%}
      {%- set wTitle = w.title or ("committee.weekly.title" | t(lang)) -%}
      {%- set wf = w | cmWeeklyFlyer(site, db.drive.items) -%}
      {#- (an online meeting, and one of the GV & LV calendars' group: "online calendar" — event-list.js facetsOf) -#}
      <li data-group="calendar" data-kind="online calendar" data-lang="{{ 'es' if w.lang == 'es' else 'en' }}" data-mode="online" x-show="show($el)">
        <article class="card ev-accent ev-tone-{{ key }} cm-event" aria-labelledby="ev-weekly-{{ key }}">
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
              {{ evm.kindBadge({}, key) }}
              <span class="badge-muted">{% icon "repeat", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.events.badge_weekly" | t(lang) }}</span>
              <span class="badge-muted">{% icon "languages", "size-3" %} {{ ("committee.weekly.lang_" + w.lang) | t(lang) }}</span>
            </div>
            <h3 id="ev-weekly-{{ key }}" class="h-card mt-2 text-lg sm:text-xl">{{ wTitle }}</h3>
            <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
              {%- set whenParts = [w.day, w.timeCentral, w.hostTime] | select %}
              {% if whenParts | length %}
              <li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "clock-3", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{% for part in whenParts %}{% if not loop.first %} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {% endif %}{{ part }}{% endfor %}</span></li>
              {% endif %}
              <li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{{ "committee.events.online_on" | t(lang, { platform: "Zoom" }) }}</span></li>
            </ul>
            {% if w.next %}
            <p class="mt-2.5 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted" data-cm-weekly="{{ w.next.iso }}" data-cm-weekly-tz="{{ w.next.tz }}"{% if w.next.at %} data-cm-weekly-at="{{ w.next.at }}"{% endif %}{% if w.starts %} data-cm-weekly-starts="{{ w.starts.iso }}"{% endif %} data-cm-weekly-len="60">
              {% icon "calendar", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}
              <span class="min-w-0">
                {%- if w.starts %}
                <span class="font-semibold text-ink" data-cm-weekly-label data-next="{{ 'committee.weekly.next' | t(lang) }}" data-live="{{ 'committee.meeting.live_now' | t(lang) }}">{{ "committee.weekly.starts" | t(lang, { date: w.starts.date }) }}</span>
                <span data-cm-weekly-date>· {{ w.starts.range }}</span>
                {%- else %}
                <span class="font-semibold text-ink" data-cm-weekly-label data-next="{{ 'committee.weekly.next' | t(lang) }}" data-live="{{ 'committee.meeting.live_now' | t(lang) }}">{{ "committee.weekly.next" | t(lang) }}</span>
                <span data-cm-weekly-date>{{ w.next.date }} · {{ w.next.range }}</span>
                {%- endif %}
                <span class="block text-xs" data-cm-weekly-local data-tpl="{{ 'committee.meeting.your_time' | t(lang) }}" hidden></span>
              </span>
            </p>
            {% endif %}
            {%- set wc = w | cmWeeklyCal(site, lang) %}
            <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,9.5rem),1fr))] gap-2 sm:flex sm:flex-wrap">
              {% if w.zoomUrl %}<a class="btn-primary btn-sm col-span-full" href="{{ w.zoomUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{ ('committee.weekly.join_' + key) | t(lang) }}">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, { platform: "Zoom" }) }}</a>{% endif %}
              <a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ '/meetings/#weekly-open' | lurl(lang) }}">{% icon "info", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.details_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "committee.events.meeting_details" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> — {{ wTitle }}</span></a>
              {% if wc %}
              <details class="cm-menu">
                <summary class="btn-secondary btn-sm w-full sm:w-auto" aria-label="{{ 'committee.weekly.cal_aria' | t(lang, { name: wTitle }) }}">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden">{{ "committee.events.cal_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:hidden">{{ "common.add_to_calendar" | t(lang) }}</span> {% icon "chevron-down", "size-4 opacity-70" %}</summary>
                <div class="cm-menu-panel max-sm:right-0 max-sm:left-auto">
                  <a href="{{ wc.gcal }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Google Calendar<span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>
                  <a href="{{ wc.ics }}" download="weekly-open-{{ wc.key }}.ics" type="text/calendar">{% icon "download", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.cal.ics_file" | t(lang) }}</a>
                  <p class="cm-menu-note">{{ "committee.cal.reminder_timed" | t(lang) }}</p>
                </div>
              </details>
              {% endif %}
              {{ ui.flyerButton(wf, wTitle, lang, "btn-secondary btn-sm" + (" col-span-full" if wc else "")) }}
            </div>
          </div>
          {{ ui.flyerThumb(wf, wTitle, lang) }}
        </article>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {#- ---------- Empty states ---------- -#}
  {#- (no event of OUR OWN: the committee meetings, NETA 65 events too, are not what this is about) -#}
  {% if nNetaOwn == 0 %}
  {#- No flyers / manual events yet: one line for visitors + a pointer to the committee how-to
      (the naming rule and the Drive folder are in "For committee members · Add an event", #how-events) -#}
  <div id="ev-empty-neta" class="mt-2" x-show="!active || group">
    {{ ui.emptyState("calendar-days", "committee.events.empty_neta_title" | t(lang), "committee.events.empty_neta_text" | t(lang), "#how-events", "committee.events.how_link" | t(lang)) }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if nCal == 0 %}
  <div class="mt-2" x-show="f.kind === 'calendar'" x-cloak>
    {{ ui.emptyState("grapes", "committee.events.empty_cal_title" | t(lang), "committee.events.empty_cal_text" | t(lang), "https://www.aagrapevine.org/get-involved/calendar", "committee.events.empty_cal_cta" | t(lang)) }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {#- ---------- Past events ---------- -#}
  {% if past | length %}
  <details class="card mt-12 group/past" data-cm-past>
    <summary class="flex min-h-14 cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-3 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
      <span class="grid size-10 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-surface-2 text-muted">{% icon "history", "size-5" %}</span>
      <h2 class="h-card flex-1 text-lg">{{ "committee.events.past" | t(lang) }} <span class="font-sans text-sm font-normal text-muted">({{ past | length }})</span></h2>
      {% icon "chevron-down", "size-5 text-muted transition group-open/past:rotate-180" %}
    </summary>
    <ol class="divide-y divide-line border-t border-line">
      {% for ev in past | limit(40) %}
      <li id="{{ ev.anchor }}" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 px-5 py-3.5 sm:px-6">{% for a in ev.item | evOldAnchors %}<span id="{{ a }}" class="sr-only"></span>{% endfor %}
        <time class="inline-flex w-32 shrink-0 items-center gap-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-muted" datetime="{{ ev.startIso }}"><span class="ev-dot ev-tone-{{ ev | eventTone }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ ev.startIso | fmtDate(lang, "short") }}</time>
        <span class="min-w-[11rem] flex-1 break-words font-medium text-ink">{{ ev.title }}{% if ev.location and not ev.locationTba %} <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted">· {{ ev.location }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
        {% if ev.flyer %}{{ ui.flyerButton(ev.flyer, ev.title, lang, "btn-ghost btn-sm") }}
        {% elif ev.link and ev.linkExternal %}{{ organizerButton(ev, "btn-ghost btn-sm") }}{% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </details>
  {% endif %}

  {#- ---------- How events get here (the three kinds of events, in visitors' words; how the
       committee adds one is in "For committee members · Add an event" below) ---------- -#}
  <section class="panel-muted mt-12" aria-labelledby="ev-src-title">
    <h2 id="ev-src-title" class="card-h"><span>{% icon "sparkles", "size-5" %}</span>{{ "committee.events.sources_title" | t(lang) }}</h2>
    <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-muted">{{ "committee.events.sources_sub" | t(lang) }}</p>
    <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      {% for s in [["meetings", "users", "bg-grape-soft text-grape"], ["flyers", "map-pin", "bg-vine-soft text-vine"], ["calendars", "grapes", "bg-lv-soft text-lv"]] %}
      <li class="flex gap-3.5">
        <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl {{ s[2] }}">{% icon s[1], "size-5" %}</span>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="h-card text-base">{{ ("committee.events.src_" + s[0]) | t(lang) }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ ("committee.events.src_" + s[0] + "_text") | t(lang, pf) }}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>

{#- ---------- The calendar subscription (#subscribe: the hero's "Subscribe" button; /meetings/, /stay-updated/ and
     Home's calendar card — when Home lists fewer than three events — link to it; cmSubscribe) — from 1024px under the
     calendar in the sidebar, below 1024px after the list ---------- -#}
<aside class="ev-side-sub min-w-0" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.aside_aria' | t(lang) }}">
  <div id="subscribe">
    {% cmSubscribe lang, site %}
  </div>
</aside>
</div>
</div>

{#- ---------- For committee members (collapsed): add an event — the two kinds of flyers in the same Drive
     folder: a name that starts with a date makes a new event; the flyer of an event already written in
     content/events gets a name WITHOUT a date and is linked from that file (`flyer:`), because a dated flyer
     and a file are never taken for the same event — dated, the event would be listed twice
     (content/events/README.md, "The flyer"). Then the folder, the naming rule with an example of each, and
     the two Drive actions (the same as the Portfolio's) ---------- -#}
{%- set exDate = "2027-03-14" | fmtDate(lang, "medium") -%}
<div class="container-page mt-12">
  {% call ui.memberHelp(lang, "committee.events.how_title" | t(lang), { id: "how-events" }) %}
  <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.2fr)] lg:gap-10">
    <div class="cm-ev-how">
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted"><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">{{ "committee.events.how_new_q" | t(lang) }}</strong> {{ "committee.events.how_text" | t(lang) }}</p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted"><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">{{ "committee.events.how_linked_q" | t(lang) }}</strong> {{ "committee.events.how_linked" | t(lang, { folder: "<code>content/events</code>", line: "<code>flyer:</code>" }) | safe }}</p>
      {% cmDrivePath lang, di, "flyers" %}
      {% if nNetaOwn == 0 %}{% cmDriveChecked lang, di %}{% endif %}
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
        {% if di.url %}<a class="btn-primary" href="{{ di.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "folder-open", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.drive.open_folder" | t(lang) }}</a>{% endif %}
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="mailto:{{ site.contact_email }}?subject={{ 'committee.docs.mail_subject' | t(lang) | urlencode }}">{% icon "mail", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.docs.ask_access" | t(lang) }}</a>
        {% if site.repository %}<a class="btn-secondary" href="{{ site.repository }}/issues/new?template=new-event.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} {{ "evlist.request" | t(lang) }}<span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cm-naming-box min-w-0">
      <div class="cm-naming" role="table" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.naming_aria' | t(lang) }}">
        <div class="cm-naming-head" role="row">
          <span role="columnheader">{{ "committee.events.naming_name" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <span role="columnheader">{{ "committee.events.naming_result" | t(lang) }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cm-naming-row" role="row">
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-file">{% icon "file-text", "size-4 shrink-0 text-lv" %}<code>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex1" | t(lang) }}</code></span>
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-out">{% icon "calendar-check", "size-4 shrink-0 text-vine" %}<span>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex1_out" | t(lang, { date: exDate }) }}</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cm-naming-row" role="row">
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-file">{% icon "file-text", "size-4 shrink-0 text-lv" %}<code>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex2" | t(lang) }}</code></span>
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-out">{% icon "calendar-check", "size-4 shrink-0 text-vine" %}<span>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex2_out" | t(lang, { date: exDate }) }}</span></span>
        </div>
        {#- no date: no event of its own — the flyer of an event already on the page, linked from its file -#}
        <div class="cm-naming-row" role="row">
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-file">{% icon "file-text", "size-4 shrink-0 text-lv" %}<code>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex3" | t(lang) }}</code></span>
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-out">{% icon "link", "size-4 shrink-0 text-vine" %}<span>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex3_out" | t(lang) }}</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ "committee.events.naming_tip" | t(lang) }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endcall %}
</div>

{% cmPreviewDialog lang %}
